<section class="faq-section section-shell" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
        <div class="faq-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</p>
          <h2 class="section-title" id="faq-title">Questions, answered before production starts.</h2>
          <p>Quick answers about product setup, artwork, approvals, and the final handoff.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details open="">
            <summary data-cursor-kind="dashboard" data-cursor-label="OPEN"><span>01</span><strong>What kinds of custom products can PromoPlus manage?</strong></summary>
            <p>Any item that needs artwork placement and approval, including apparel, bags, drinkware, signage, packaging, and more.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary data-cursor-kind="dashboard" data-cursor-label="OPEN"><span>02</span><strong>Can each product side be approved separately?</strong></summary>
            <p>Yes. Front, Back, Sleeve, or any custom surface can keep its own artwork, comments, version, and approval status.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary data-cursor-kind="approval" data-cursor-label="APPROVE"><span>03</span><strong>How do clients review and approve a mockup?</strong></summary>
            <p>One shareable review link lets a client view the current mockup, leave comments, request changes, or approve the version.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary data-cursor-kind="version" data-cursor-label="COMPARE"><span>04</span><strong>What happens when the artwork changes?</strong></summary>
            <p>Every revision remains connected to its product side, comments, and status, so the latest approved version is always clear.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary data-cursor-kind="dashboard" data-cursor-label="OPEN"><span>05</span><strong>What is included in the production-ready file?</strong></summary>
            <p>The final handoff brings together the approved mockup, artwork, product sides, version, approver, and timestamp in one PDF.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

